                <pb facs="0776" n="678" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg678"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/2921: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Guggenheim</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-11T17:00:00-05:00">December 11, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:07 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>163. My 146, November 26, 2 p.m. This afternoon President Machado signed the bill
                    authorizing him to suspend constitutional guarantees, and simultaneously
                    suspension of the constitutional guarantees was decreed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Guggenheim</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
